      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a beach bucket with a spade and a starfish sand mould. Draw it as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate pieces laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every piece at the size it has in image 1 (if they do not all fit, draw them all a little smaller, at the same scale as each other).\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no piece touching or overlapping another:\n1. the red bucket with its yellow handle, EMPTY: no spade and no starfish mould, drawn whole, including the part the starfish hides in image 1; its open top shows the inside of the bucket.\n2. the bucket's front rim alone: only the thick rolled red lip along the near (front) half of the bucket's round opening, a thin curved band, as it is in image 1.\n3. the blue plastic spade alone, whole: its handle with the grip hole and its whole blade, including the part hidden inside the bucket in image 1.\n4. the same blue spade with a small heap of golden sand piled on its blade.\n5. the green starfish-shaped sand mould alone, whole.\n\nEvery piece is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another piece, with its edges clean and smooth. It is an object, not a character: no face, no eyes, no mouth. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the pieces beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows, no water, no sand, no splashes or drops. Fully transparent background."
    },
