      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a red beach bucket with a spade in it; image 2 shows the bucket cut into puppet pieces. Draw ONE piece on its own, at the size the bucket has in image 2 (piece 1, top left), the same drawing style, colours, texture and line: the front of the red bucket — its outer wall, its yellow handle and the near (front) half of its rolled rim — with everything above the front rim cut away: no inside of the bucket, no back rim. Its top edge is the upper edge of the front rim, a smooth downward curve, so that something standing in the bucket would show above it. No spade, no starfish mould. It is an object, not a character: no face, no eyes, no mouth. No text, no labels, no shadows, no sand. Fully transparent background."
